# Language

## English

Write these in English:

- Code: identifiers, docstrings, comments, exception messages
- Tests: names, assertion messages
- `.cursor/` rules and skills, `.github/` template headings
- Commit `type` and `scope`, PR titles' type and scope
- `docs/roadmap.md`. It has no Japanese copy; the owner dropped `docs/roadmap.ja.md` as not needed (#37)

Chat with the owner is in Japanese, including reports and Grill questions. Issue bodies, PR bodies, and commit subjects may be Japanese.

## User and internal docs

- `README.md` and `README.ja.md` are the bilingual pair. English is the source of truth. Change both files in the same PR. Headings stay English. Keep the language switch line at the top of both files.
- `docs/tutorials.md`, `docs/how-to.md`, `docs/reference.md`, and `docs/explanation.md` are the user-facing Diataxis documents, in Japanese.
- `docs/conventions.md`, `docs/roadmap.md`, and `docs/adr/` are internal developer documents, in English. Do not add Japanese copies of internal docs or `CONTRIBUTING.md`. The owner's process is `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/`.
